# The ONLY per-branch file in the benchmark harness.
#
# Everything under k6/ and docker-compose.bench.yml is byte-identical on all eight variant
# branches, with ES-4 as the reference. The acceptance test:
#     git diff --stat ES-4 <branch> -- k6 docker-compose.bench.yml
# must print nothing. No exclusions: the three superseded planning docs that used to
# force a path list (k6/load-tests-plan.md and the two ES-4-local campaign notes) are
# gone. The campaign runbook on `main` supersedes them.
#
# Branch: ES-4-parallel  (ES-4 with the order saga dispatching every line's reserve command at
# once instead of one after the next — see CLAUDE.md. ONE variable against ES-4, which since
# 2026-09-04 carries the mark-and-resolve cache this branch also has; everything else is ES-4:
# Axon 4.11.2, LOCK-FREE aggregate access (NullLockFactory) + the copy-on-write cache. Its A/B
# partner is the ES-4 branch, whose runs file under VARIANT=ES-4-NullLock; the same port on the
# uncached baseline is ES-2-parallel, which is the row that isolates the cache from the dispatch
# shape.)
#
# VARIANT is what names the run directory and the thesis-table row (bench.sh builds
# RUN_NAME from it, NOT from the git branch), so a stale value here silently files this
# branch's results under another variant.

VARIANT=ES-4-parallel
VARIANT_FAMILY=ES

# docker compose service names (differ between the TO and ES families)
API_SVC=api-es
DB_SVC=postgres-es

# Prometheus job label for this branch's API target, and the cadvisor container-name regex.
# The regex must stay UNANCHORED: the API service is scaled with deploy.replicas and so
# carries no container_name, which means cadvisor sees `<project>-api-es-1`, `-2`, ...
# rather than a bare `api-es`. queries.promql matches it with an anchored name=~"$CRE".
#
# EXPECTED_REPLICAS is NOT set here. common.sh derives it from REPLICAS in .env, which is
# the file docker compose actually acts on — one knob, not two.
PROM_JOB=inventory-es
API_CONTAINER_RE=.*api-es.*

DB_NAME=inventory
DB_USER=inventory

# Health endpoint on the published port, which on every branch is nginx in front of the
# api replicas. At REPLICAS>1 a healthy response only proves that ONE replica answered —
# reset.sh asserts the full container count separately.
HEALTH_URL=http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

# Image bench.sh builds and tags before each run, and the tag docker-compose.yml
# substitutes into the api service. UNIQUE PER VARIANT, not per family: ES-2 and ES-4 once
# shared inventory-reservation-es:latest and TO-1..TO-4 shared the -to one, so building any
# variant silently overwrote its sibling's image. common.sh exports this, and Compose
# prefers the shell environment over .env, so the harness and a bare `docker compose up`
# always agree on which image runs.
IMAGE_TAG=inventory-reservation-es-4-parallel:latest
